cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SSEE — Structural Self-Energy Expansion (V3.6)"
abstract: >
  A minimal-parameter dark energy framework derived algebraically from φ (golden ratio)
  and π. Ten papers spanning: algebraic framework (w₀, wₐ, EFT, Predictive Register),
  Bayesian MCMC validation (DESI DR2 + Planck + clusters), CMB confrontation (Planck PR4
  TT+TE+EE+lensing; full plik MCMC ΔBIC=−32.9, k=2 vs k=6), algebraic derivation of CMB observables from φ and π,
  Israel-Stewart causal perturbation theory (gradient stability, ΛCDM-consistent growth, S₈),
  φ-Dark Matter two-sector model (m_φ=40.70 eV algebraic via SOLAR²·KRYSTOS, S₈=0.758 at 0.04σ KiDS, fσ₈ 0.93σ two-sector),
  canonical EFT (β_c=−AURA exact, αT=αM=αB=0 exact, αK=0.403 algebraic),
  strong-gravity regime (disformal geodesics, k-mouflage screening),
  Hubble-tension screening fraction f_screen=αK/(3·MIRA), and UV completion
  K(X)=X/KAL+X²/M⁴ with M=9.68 meV.
